The original calls `GetName()` and `GetNumSubFields()` repeatedly inside nested loops. The version below hoists the per-field reference and subfield count out of the inner loop, so the field lookup and count run once per field instead of once per subfield iteration. Matching order, short-circuit behavior, the 16-bit index type, and return values are unchanged. The gain is modest, since the per-call string copies in the getters (which I can't see here) remain.

```cpp
const Field* Mesg::GetField(const std::string& name) const
{
    const FIT_UINT16 count = (FIT_UINT16)fields.size();
    for (FIT_UINT16 i = 0; i < count; i++)
    {
        const Field& f = fields[i];
        if (f.GetName() == name)
            return &fields[i];

        const FIT_UINT16 numSub = f.GetNumSubFields();
        for (FIT_UINT16 j = 0; j < numSub; j++)
        {
            if ((f.GetName(j) == name) && CanSupportSubField(&fields[i], j))
                return &fields[i];
        }
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```

